Why vendored: the workload build is JDK-only (no Maven or Gradle) and must
work offline. The core workload stays free of third-party code
(docs/decisions.md #5); only this separate module's jar, workload-otel.jar,
runs against these jars, named in its manifest's Class-Path, not copied
into it. `mage workloadOtelBuild` checks the SHA-256s above before
compiling.

Why the API and not the SDK: the Java agent reads the active span through
the API (Span.current(), docs/implementation.md M3 step 8), and the golden
needs ids it can declare. Span.wrap(SpanContext.create(...)).makeCurrent()
gives both with the API alone; an SDK would draw random ids.

Why this version: 1.67.0 is the newest release at least two weeks old on
the fetch date (1.68.0 was 13 days old); the API is Java 8 bytecode, so it
runs on the workload's Java 21 floor.

